<% content_for :title, "Privacy" %>
<% contact = ENV["SUPPORT_EMAIL"].presence %>

<article class="narrow privacy-page">
  <header class="page-header">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>Last updated November 8, 2026.</p>
  </header>

  <p>
    Bookem lets people book time at local businesses, and lets those businesses
    take bookings. This page explains what we collect, why, and how to have it deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul class="plain-list">
    <li><strong>Your account:</strong> your name, email address and password (stored encrypted). Optional: phone number, organization and website.</li>
    <li><strong>Bookings:</strong> the times you request, the services you choose, and their status.</li>
    <li><strong>Locations you list:</strong> the name, address, hours, services, prices and photos you add.</li>
    <li><strong>Payments:</strong> deposits are paid on Stripe's own pages. We never see or store card numbers. Stripe tells us whether a payment went through.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who sees it</h2>
  <ul class="plain-list">
    <li>A booking is visible only to the guest who made it and the business it's with.</li>
    <li>Location pages are public, but they never show who booked a time.</li>
    <li>We use service providers to run Bookem: Render (hosting), Stripe (payments), Cloudinary (photos) and Mapbox (maps). They only get what they need to do that job.</li>
    <li>We don't sell your information or use it for advertising.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Deleting your account</h2>
  <p>
    You can delete your account at any time from
    <%= link_to "Edit profile", edit_user_registration_path %>, on the web or in the app.
    This deletes your account, your locations and your bookings. Payment records
    that Stripe must keep by law stay with Stripe.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <% if contact %>
      Questions about your information? Email <%= mail_to contact %>.
    <% else %>
      Questions about your information? Use the contact email on Bookem's App Store or Google Play page.
    <% end %>
  </p>
</article>
